 ## Background
-Chunked Otsu Thresholding was introduced as part of a pull request to the `pymedphys` project to address memory issues in surface rendering and contour sheet generation [S1, unofficial]. It is an optimization of the existing Otsu thresholding implementation, which previously required copying the entire volume to `float64`, leading to high memory peaks [S1, unofficial]. The method leverages the deterministic nature of histogram binning to allow partial counts to be summed, enabling efficient processing of large datasets [S1, unofficial].
